### Microsoft PowerToys version and release channel

`main` @ 6896d763 (built from source)

### Installation method

Built from source (GitHub)

### Running as admin

No

### Area(s) with issue?

Peek

### Steps to reproduce

Code-level defect, found by inspection rather than a reliable UI repro — the crash depends on the temp-directory cleanup throwing.

`src/modules/peek/Peek.FilePreviewer/Previewers/WebBrowserPreviewer/WebBrowserPreviewer.cs`:

```csharp
~WebBrowserPreviewer()
{
    Dispose(false);
}

public void Dispose()
{
    Dispose(true);
    GC.SuppressFinalize(this);
}

protected virtual async void Dispose(bool disposing)
{
    if (!this.disposed)
    {
        await Microsoft.PowerToys.FilePreviewCommon.Helper.CleanupTempDirAsync(TempFolderPath.Path);
        disposed = true;
    }
}
```

### ✔️ Expected Behavior

Disposing a `WebBrowserPreviewer` cleans up its temp files and any failure stays contained.

### ❌ Actual Behavior

An exception during cleanup can terminate the PowerToys process, and disposal is not deterministic.

### Additional Information

Two problems with the `async void` signature:

1. **Process crash path.** An `async void` method resumes on the thread pool after its first `await`; an exception thrown past that point is raised as an unhandled exception instead of surfacing to the caller. Since the finalizer calls `Dispose(false)`, there is no caller to surface it to at all.
2. **Non-deterministic disposal.** `Dispose()` returns as soon as the `await` is reached, so the object reports itself disposed while cleanup is still in flight, and `disposed` is only set afterwards — a second `Dispose()` in that window re-runs the cleanup.

The `disposing` argument is ignored entirely, so the finalizer path performs the same managed cleanup as the explicit path.

The awaited call does no real asynchronous work: `Helper.CleanupTempDirAsync` is `Task.Run(() => CleanupTempDir(folder))`, and `CleanupTempDir` already swallows its own exceptions.

**Proposed fix.** Make `Dispose(bool)` synchronous and perform cleanup only when `disposing` is true — the canonical dispose pattern. `MarkdownPreviewHandlerControl` already calls `Helper.CleanupTempDir` synchronously from its dispose path, so this also makes the two previewers consistent.

I have a fix ready and am happy to open a PR if the approach looks right.
